<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 90-day T-bill yields avg 2.875 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 90-day T-bill yields avg 2.875 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.3 billion of 90-day Government of Canada treasury bills due March 27, 1997 was 2.875 percent, down from 3.036 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.1 billion of 174-day T-bills due June 19, 1997 was 3.257 percent, down from 3.379 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 361-day T-bills due December  23, 1997 was 3.607 percent, down from 3.812 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$700 million three-month, C$200 million six-month and C$175 million one-year bills. It holds C$975 million of C$4.5 million bills due January 3. (Details follow)</p>
